# A synthetic RTL translation of Virtaal's own UI catalog (po/virtaal.pot),
# for testing whether the app's whole chrome (menus, toolbar, panels - not
# just editor text) actually mirrors under a right-to-left UI language.
# Dwayne's suggestion, 2026-08-25, as the fuller version of testing bidi
# support - devsupport/testfiles/rtl.po covers RTL *content* inside the
# editor; this covers RTL *layout*, a currently entirely untested,
# different risk area.
#
# Generated via translate-toolkit's own podebug (--rewrite=flipped, same
# mechanism as rtl.po - see that file's own header for what it does and
# why), run against po/virtaal.pot directly rather than any real
# community translation, so it has full, current coverage of every UI
# string - not a real language, deliberately: legible-ish (flipped
# Unicode glyphs) for a non-Arabic/Farsi-reading developer to sanity-check
# against the real English UI, unlike real Arabic/Farsi content would be.
#
# Tagged Language: fa (Farsi/Persian) rather than the more obvious `ar` -
# both are genuinely RTL-recognised by GTK/Pango's own language-direction
# tables, but `ar` already ships a real community translation (po/ar.po,
# listed in po/LINGUAS) that this would otherwise shadow/clobber if
# compiled into the same installed slot; `fa` has no real Virtaal
# translation at all, so there's nothing to collide with.
#
# NOT a real translation - never add to po/LINGUAS or ship this in a
# release build. Compile with translate.tools.pocompile.convertmo (same
# pure-Python compiler setup.py's own mo-compile step uses, no external
# msgfmt needed) into share/locale/fa/LC_MESSAGES/virtaal.mo relative to
# a virtaal.exe, then launch with LANG=fa_IR.UTF-8/LANGUAGE=fa - see
# devsupport/testing/windows/Enable-VirtaalRtlDebug.ps1 for the actual
# Windows procedure (the only platform whose frozen build has the
# fix_libintl locale-binding this needs already wired up and exercised -
# see virtaal/common/pan_app.py). Regenerate by re-running podebug
# against a fresh po/virtaal.pot and re-applying this same header fixup
# (Language: fa, clear the header's own fuzzy flag, a real Plural-Forms
# line) if virtaal's own UI strings change enough to matter.
#
# Copyright (C) YEAR Zuza Software Foundation (Translate.org.za)
# This file is distributed under the same license as the Virtaal package.
