#: ../virtaal/support/native_widgets.py:180
#: ../virtaal/support/native_widgets.py:249 ../virtaal/views/mainview.py:275
msgid "Choose a Translation File"
msgstr "‮Ↄɥoosǝ ɐ ⊥ɹɐusʅɐʇıou Ⅎıʅǝ"

#: ../virtaal/support/native_widgets.py:160
msgid ""
"A file named \"%1\" already exists. Are you sure you want to overwrite it?"
msgstr ""
"‮∀ ɟıʅǝ uɐɯǝp „%1‮„ ɐʅɹǝɐpʎ ǝxısʇs˙ ∀ɹǝ ʎon snɹǝ ʎon ʍɐuʇ ʇo oʌǝɹʍɹıʇǝ ıʇ¿"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:38
msgid ""
"Welcome to the Virtaal tutorial. You can do the first translation by typing "
"just the translation for \"Welcome\". Then press Enter."
msgstr ""
"‮Ｍǝʅɔoɯǝ ʇo ʇɥǝ Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ ʇnʇoɹıɐʅ˙ ⅄on ɔɐu po ʇɥǝ ɟıɹsʇ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou qʎ ʇʎdıuƃ "
"ɾnsʇ ʇɥǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɟoɹ „Ｍǝʅɔoɯǝ„˙ ⊥ɥǝu dɹǝss Ǝuʇǝɹ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:43
msgid ""
"Translate this slightly longer message. If a spell checker is available, "
"spelling mistakes are indicated similarly to word processors. Make sure the "
"correct language is selected in the bottom right of the window."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ʇɥıs sʅıƃɥʇʅʎ ʅouƃǝɹ ɯǝssɐƃǝ˙ Iɟ ɐ sdǝʅʅ ɔɥǝɔʞǝɹ ıs ɐʌɐıʅɐqʅǝ´ "
"sdǝʅʅıuƃ ɯısʇɐʞǝs ɐɹǝ ıupıɔɐʇǝp sıɯıʅɐɹʅʎ ʇo ʍoɹp dɹoɔǝssoɹs˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʇɥǝ "
"ɔoɹɹǝɔʇ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ ıs sǝʅǝɔʇǝp ıu ʇɥǝ qoʇʇoɯ ɹıƃɥʇ oɟ ʇɥǝ ʍıupoʍ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:50
msgid ""
"This tutorial will show you some of the things you might want to pay "
"attention to while translating software programs. It will help you to avoid "
"some problems and produce translations of a higher quality."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ʇnʇoɹıɐʅ ʍıʅʅ sɥoʍ ʎon soɯǝ oɟ ʇɥǝ ʇɥıuƃs ʎon ɯıƃɥʇ ʍɐuʇ ʇo dɐʎ "
"ɐʇʇǝuʇıou ʇo ʍɥıʅǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıuƃ soɟʇʍɐɹǝ dɹoƃɹɐɯs˙ Iʇ ʍıʅʅ ɥǝʅd ʎon ʇo ɐʌoıp "
"soɯǝ dɹoqʅǝɯs ɐup dɹopnɔǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıous oɟ ɐ ɥıƃɥǝɹ bnɐʅıʇʎ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:57
msgid ""
"Some of the advice will only be relevant to some languages. For example, if "
"your language does not use the Latin alphabet, some of the advice might not "
"be relevant to translation in your language. For many languages there are "
"established translation rules."
msgstr ""
"‮Soɯǝ oɟ ʇɥǝ ɐpʌıɔǝ ʍıʅʅ ouʅʎ qǝ ɹǝʅǝʌɐuʇ ʇo soɯǝ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝs˙ Ⅎoɹ ǝxɐɯdʅǝ´ ıɟ "
"ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ poǝs uoʇ nsǝ ʇɥǝ ⅂ɐʇıu ɐʅdɥɐqǝʇ´ soɯǝ oɟ ʇɥǝ ɐpʌıɔǝ ɯıƃɥʇ uoʇ "
"qǝ ɹǝʅǝʌɐuʇ ʇo ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ıu ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ˙ Ⅎoɹ ɯɐuʎ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝs ʇɥǝɹǝ ɐɹǝ "
"ǝsʇɐqʅısɥǝp ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɹnʅǝs˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:64
msgid ""
"The correct use of capital letters are important in many languages. "
"Translate this message with careful attention to write \"Virtaal\" with a "
"capital letter."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥǝ ɔoɹɹǝɔʇ nsǝ oɟ ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹs ɐɹǝ ıɯdoɹʇɐuʇ ıu ɯɐuʎ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝs˙ ⊥"
"ɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʍıʇɥ ɔɐɹǝɟnʅ ɐʇʇǝuʇıou ʇo ʍɹıʇǝ „Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ„ ʍıʇɥ ɐ "
"ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:70
msgid ""
"In this message the English uses a capital letter for almost every word. "
"Almost no other language uses this style. Unless your language definitely "
"needs to follow the English style (also called Title Case), translate this "
"by following the normal capitalisation rules for your language. If your "
"language does not use capital letters, simply translate it normally."
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʇɥǝ Ǝuƃʅısɥ nsǝs ɐ ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹ ɟoɹ ɐʅɯosʇ ǝʌǝɹʎ ʍoɹp˙ ∀"
"ʅɯosʇ uo oʇɥǝɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ nsǝs ʇɥıs sʇʎʅǝ˙ ∩uʅǝss ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ pǝɟıuıʇǝʅʎ "
"uǝǝps ʇo ɟoʅʅoʍ ʇɥǝ Ǝuƃʅısɥ sʇʎʅǝ (ɐʅso ɔɐʅʅǝp ⊥ıʇʅǝ Ↄɐsǝ)´ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ʇɥıs "
"qʎ ɟoʅʅoʍıuƃ ʇɥǝ uoɹɯɐʅ ɔɐdıʇɐʅısɐʇıou ɹnʅǝs ɟoɹ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ˙ Iɟ ʎonɹ "
"ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ poǝs uoʇ nsǝ ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹs´ sıɯdʅʎ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ıʇ uoɹɯɐʅʅʎ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:79
msgid ""
"If you translated the previous message you should see a window with that "
"translation and a percentage indicating how similar the source strings "
"(English) are. It is Virtaal's translation memory at work. Press Ctrl+1 to "
"copy the suggested translation to the current translation. Remember to "
"always review suggestions before you use them."
msgstr ""
"‮Iɟ ʎon ʇɹɐusʅɐʇǝp ʇɥǝ dɹǝʌıons ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʎon sɥonʅp sǝǝ ɐ ʍıupoʍ ʍıʇɥ ʇɥɐʇ "
"ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɐup ɐ dǝɹɔǝuʇɐƃǝ ıupıɔɐʇıuƃ ɥoʍ sıɯıʅɐɹ ʇɥǝ sonɹɔǝ sʇɹıuƃs "
"(Ǝuƃʅısɥ) ɐɹǝ˙ Iʇ ıs Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ,s ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɯǝɯoɹʎ ɐʇ ʍoɹʞ˙ Ԁɹǝss Ↄʇɹʅ+1‮ ʇo "
"ɔodʎ ʇɥǝ snƃƃǝsʇǝp ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ʇo ʇɥǝ ɔnɹɹǝuʇ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou˙ ᴚǝɯǝɯqǝɹ ʇo "
"ɐʅʍɐʎs ɹǝʌıǝʍ snƃƃǝsʇıous qǝɟoɹǝ ʎon nsǝ ʇɥǝɯ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:88
msgid ""
"This is a simple message that starts with a capital letter in English. If "
"your language uses capital letters, you almost definitely want to start your "
"translation with a capital letter as well."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ıs ɐ sıɯdʅǝ ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʇɥɐʇ sʇɐɹʇs ʍıʇɥ ɐ ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹ ıu Ǝuƃʅısɥ˙ Iɟ "
"ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ nsǝs ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹs´ ʎon ɐʅɯosʇ pǝɟıuıʇǝʅʎ ʍɐuʇ ʇo sʇɐɹʇ ʎonɹ "
"ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ʍıʇɥ ɐ ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹ ɐs ʍǝʅʅ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:95
msgid ""
"This is a simple message that starts with a lower case letter in English. If "
"your language uses capital letters, you almost definitely want to start your "
"translation with a lower case letter as well."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ıs ɐ sıɯdʅǝ ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʇɥɐʇ sʇɐɹʇs ʍıʇɥ ɐ ʅoʍǝɹ ɔɐsǝ ʅǝʇʇǝɹ ıu Ǝuƃʅısɥ˙ Iɟ "
"ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ nsǝs ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹs´ ʎon ɐʅɯosʇ pǝɟıuıʇǝʅʎ ʍɐuʇ ʇo sʇɐɹʇ ʎonɹ "
"ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ʍıʇɥ ɐ ʅoʍǝɹ ɔɐsǝ ʅǝʇʇǝɹ ɐs ʍǝʅʅ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:102
msgid ""
"This message is a question. Make sure that you use the correct question mark "
"in your translation as well."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ıs ɐ bnǝsʇıou˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʇɥɐʇ ʎon nsǝ ʇɥǝ ɔoɹɹǝɔʇ bnǝsʇıou ɯɐɹʞ "
"ıu ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɐs ʍǝʅʅ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:107
msgid ""
"This message is a label as part of a form. Note how it ends with a colon (:)."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ıs ɐ ʅɐqǝʅ ɐs dɐɹʇ oɟ ɐ ɟoɹɯ˙ Noʇǝ ɥoʍ ıʇ ǝups ʍıʇɥ ɐ ɔoʅou (:)˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:112
msgid ""
"If the source will remain mostly or completely unchanged it is convenient to "
"copy the entire source string with Alt+Down. Here is almost nothing to "
"translate, so just press Alt+Down and make corrections if necessary."
msgstr ""
"‮Iɟ ʇɥǝ sonɹɔǝ ʍıʅʅ ɹǝɯɐıu ɯosʇʅʎ oɹ ɔoɯdʅǝʇǝʅʎ nuɔɥɐuƃǝp ıʇ ıs ɔouʌǝuıǝuʇ ʇo "
"ɔodʎ ʇɥǝ ǝuʇıɹǝ sonɹɔǝ sʇɹıuƃ ʍıʇɥ ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu˙ Hǝɹǝ ıs ɐʅɯosʇ uoʇɥıuƃ ʇo "
"ʇɹɐusʅɐʇǝ´ so ɾnsʇ dɹǝss ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu ɐup ɯɐʞǝ ɔoɹɹǝɔʇıous ıɟ uǝɔǝssɐɹʎ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:119
msgid ""
"Placeables are special parts of the text, like the © symbol, that can be "
"automatically highlighted and easily inserted into the translation. Select "
"the © with Alt+Right and transfer it to the target with Alt+Down."
msgstr ""
"‮Ԁʅɐɔǝɐqʅǝs ɐɹǝ sdǝɔıɐʅ dɐɹʇs oɟ ʇɥǝ ʇǝxʇ´ ʅıʞǝ ʇɥǝ ©‮ sʎɯqoʅ´ ʇɥɐʇ ɔɐu qǝ "
"ɐnʇoɯɐʇıɔɐʅʅʎ ɥıƃɥʅıƃɥʇǝp ɐup ǝɐsıʅʎ ıusǝɹʇǝp ıuʇo ʇɥǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou˙ Sǝʅǝɔʇ "
"ʇɥǝ ©‮ ʍıʇɥ ∀ʅʇ+ᴚıƃɥʇ ɐup ʇɹɐusɟǝɹ ıʇ ʇo ʇɥǝ ʇɐɹƃǝʇ ʍıʇɥ ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:126
msgid ""
"Recognised placeables include special symbols, numbers, variable "
"placeholders, acronyms and many more. Move to each one with Alt+Right and "
"transfer it down with Alt+Down."
msgstr ""
"‮ᴚǝɔoƃuısǝp dʅɐɔǝɐqʅǝs ıuɔʅnpǝ sdǝɔıɐʅ sʎɯqoʅs´ unɯqǝɹs´ ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ dʅɐɔǝɥoʅpǝɹs"
"´ ɐɔɹouʎɯs ɐup ɯɐuʎ ɯoɹǝ˙ Woʌǝ ʇo ǝɐɔɥ ouǝ ʍıʇɥ ∀ʅʇ+ᴚıƃɥʇ ɐup ʇɹɐusɟǝɹ ıʇ "
"poʍu ʍıʇɥ ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:132
msgid ""
"This message ends with ... to indicate that clicking on this text will cause "
"a dialogue to appear instead of just performing an action. Be sure to end "
"your message with ... as well."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ǝups ʍıʇɥ ˙˙˙ ʇo ıupıɔɐʇǝ ʇɥɐʇ ɔʅıɔʞıuƃ ou ʇɥıs ʇǝxʇ ʍıʅʅ ɔɐnsǝ "
"ɐ pıɐʅoƃnǝ ʇo ɐddǝɐɹ ıusʇǝɐp oɟ ɾnsʇ dǝɹɟoɹɯıuƃ ɐu ɐɔʇıou˙ Ԑǝ snɹǝ ʇo ǝup "
"ʎonɹ ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʍıʇɥ ˙˙˙ ɐs ʍǝʅʅ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:138
msgid ""
"This message ends with a special character that looks like three dots. "
"Select the special character with Alt+Right and copy it to your translation "
"with Alt+Down. Don't just type three dot characters."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ǝups ʍıʇɥ ɐ sdǝɔıɐʅ ɔɥɐɹɐɔʇǝɹ ʇɥɐʇ ʅooʞs ʅıʞǝ ʇɥɹǝǝ poʇs˙ "
"Sǝʅǝɔʇ ʇɥǝ sdǝɔıɐʅ ɔɥɐɹɐɔʇǝɹ ʍıʇɥ ∀ʅʇ+ᴚıƃɥʇ ɐup ɔodʎ ıʇ ʇo ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou "
"ʍıʇɥ ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu˙ ᗡou,ʇ ɾnsʇ ʇʎdǝ ʇɥɹǝǝ poʇ ɔɥɐɹɐɔʇǝɹs˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:145
msgid ""
"This message has two sentences. Translate them and make sure you start each "
"with a capital letter if your language uses them, and end each sentence "
"properly."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɥɐs ʇʍo sǝuʇǝuɔǝs˙ ⊥ɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ʇɥǝɯ ɐup ɯɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎon sʇɐɹʇ ǝɐɔɥ "
"ʍıʇɥ ɐ ɔɐdıʇɐʅ ʅǝʇʇǝɹ ıɟ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ nsǝs ʇɥǝɯ´ ɐup ǝup ǝɐɔɥ sǝuʇǝuɔǝ "
"dɹodǝɹʅʎ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:151
msgid ""
"This message marks the word \"now\" as important with bold tags. These tags "
"can be transferred from the source with Alt+Right and Alt+Down. Leave the "
"<b> and </b> in the translation around the part that corresponds to \"now\". "
"Read more about XML markup here: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XML"
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɯɐɹʞs ʇɥǝ ʍoɹp „uoʍ„ ɐs ıɯdoɹʇɐuʇ ʍıʇɥ qoʅp ʇɐƃs˙ ⊥ɥǝsǝ ʇɐƃs "
"ɔɐu qǝ ʇɹɐusɟǝɹɹǝp ɟɹoɯ ʇɥǝ sonɹɔǝ ʍıʇɥ ∀ʅʇ+ᴚıƃɥʇ ɐup ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu˙ ⅂ǝɐʌǝ ʇɥǝ "
"<b>‮ ɐup </b>‮ ıu ʇɥǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɐɹonup ʇɥǝ dɐɹʇ ʇɥɐʇ ɔoɹɹǝsdoups ʇo „uoʍ„˙ "
"ᴚǝɐp ɯoɹǝ ɐqonʇ XW⅂ ɯɐɹʞnd ɥǝɹǝ: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XML"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:159
msgid ""
"This message is very similar to the previous message. Use the suggestion of "
"the previous translation with Ctrl+1. Note how the only difference is that "
"this one ends with a full stop after the last tag."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ıs ʌǝɹʎ sıɯıʅɐɹ ʇo ʇɥǝ dɹǝʌıons ɯǝssɐƃǝ˙ ∩sǝ ʇɥǝ snƃƃǝsʇıou oɟ "
"ʇɥǝ dɹǝʌıons ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ʍıʇɥ Ↄʇɹʅ+1‮˙ Noʇǝ ɥoʍ ʇɥǝ ouʅʎ pıɟɟǝɹǝuɔǝ ıs ʇɥɐʇ "
"ʇɥıs ouǝ ǝups ʍıʇɥ ɐ ɟnʅʅ sʇod ɐɟʇǝɹ ʇɥǝ ʅɐsʇ ʇɐƃ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:166
#, python-format
msgid ""
"In this message \"%d\" is a placeholder (variable) that represents a number. "
"Make sure your translation contains \"%d\" somewhere. In this case it refers "
"a number of files. When this message is used the \"%d\" will be replaced "
"with a number e.g. 'Number of files copied: 5'.  Note that \"%d\" does not "
"refer to a percentage."
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ „%d‮„ ıs ɐ dʅɐɔǝɥoʅpǝɹ (ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ) ʇɥɐʇ ɹǝdɹǝsǝuʇs ɐ unɯqǝɹ˙ "
"Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɔouʇɐıus „%d‮„ soɯǝʍɥǝɹǝ˙ Iu ʇɥıs ɔɐsǝ ıʇ ɹǝɟǝɹs ɐ "
"unɯqǝɹ oɟ ɟıʅǝs˙ Ｍɥǝu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ıs nsǝp ʇɥǝ „%d‮„ ʍıʅʅ qǝ ɹǝdʅɐɔǝp ʍıʇɥ ɐ "
"unɯqǝɹ ǝ˙ƃ˙ ,Nnɯqǝɹ oɟ ɟıʅǝs ɔodıǝp: 5‮,˙  Noʇǝ ʇɥɐʇ „%d‮„ poǝs uoʇ ɹǝɟǝɹ ʇo ɐ "
"dǝɹɔǝuʇɐƃǝ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:174
#, python-format
msgid ""
"In this message, \"%d\" refers again to the number of files, but note how "
"the \"(s)\" is used to show that we don't know how many it will be. This is "
"often hard to translate well. If you encounter this in software translation, "
"you might want to hear from developers if this can be avoided. Read more "
"about this and decide how to do it in your language: http://"
"docs.translatehouse.org/projects/localization-guide/en/latest/guide/"
"translation/plurals.html"
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ´ „%d‮„ ɹǝɟǝɹs ɐƃɐıu ʇo ʇɥǝ unɯqǝɹ oɟ ɟıʅǝs´ qnʇ uoʇǝ ɥoʍ ʇɥǝ „"
"(s)„ ıs nsǝp ʇo sɥoʍ ʇɥɐʇ ʍǝ pou,ʇ ʞuoʍ ɥoʍ ɯɐuʎ ıʇ ʍıʅʅ qǝ˙ ⊥ɥıs ıs oɟʇǝu "
"ɥɐɹp ʇo ʇɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ʍǝʅʅ˙ Iɟ ʎon ǝuɔonuʇǝɹ ʇɥıs ıu soɟʇʍɐɹǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou´ ʎon "
"ɯıƃɥʇ ʍɐuʇ ʇo ɥǝɐɹ ɟɹoɯ pǝʌǝʅodǝɹs ıɟ ʇɥıs ɔɐu qǝ ɐʌoıpǝp˙ ᴚǝɐp ɯoɹǝ ɐqonʇ "
"ʇɥıs ɐup pǝɔıpǝ ɥoʍ ʇo po ıʇ ıu ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ: http://"
"docs.translatehouse.org/projects/localization-guide/en/latest/guide/"
"translation/plurals.html"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:185
msgid ""
"In this message the proper way of translating plurals are seen. You need to "
"enter between 1 and 6 different versions of the translation to ensure the "
"correct grammar in your language. Read more about this here: http://"
"docs.translatehouse.org/projects/localization-guide/en/latest/guide/"
"translation/plurals.html"
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʇɥǝ dɹodǝɹ ʍɐʎ oɟ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıuƃ dʅnɹɐʅs ɐɹǝ sǝǝu˙ ⅄on uǝǝp ʇo "
"ǝuʇǝɹ qǝʇʍǝǝu 1‮ ɐup 6‮ pıɟɟǝɹǝuʇ ʌǝɹsıous oɟ ʇɥǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ʇo ǝusnɹǝ ʇɥǝ "
"ɔoɹɹǝɔʇ ƃɹɐɯɯɐɹ ıu ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ˙ ᴚǝɐp ɯoɹǝ ɐqonʇ ʇɥıs ɥǝɹǝ: http://"
"docs.translatehouse.org/projects/localization-guide/en/latest/guide/"
"translation/plurals.html"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:196
#, python-format
msgid ""
"In this message, \"%s\" is a placeholder (variable) that represents a file "
"name. Make sure your translation contains %s somewhere. When this message is "
"used, the %s will be replaced with a file name e.g. 'The file will be saved "
"as example.odt'.  Note that \"%s\" does not refer to a percentage."
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ´ „%s‮„ ıs ɐ dʅɐɔǝɥoʅpǝɹ (ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ) ʇɥɐʇ ɹǝdɹǝsǝuʇs ɐ ɟıʅǝ uɐɯǝ"
"˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɔouʇɐıus %s‮ soɯǝʍɥǝɹǝ˙ Ｍɥǝu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ıs "
"nsǝp´ ʇɥǝ %s‮ ʍıʅʅ qǝ ɹǝdʅɐɔǝp ʍıʇɥ ɐ ɟıʅǝ uɐɯǝ ǝ˙ƃ˙ ,⊥ɥǝ ɟıʅǝ ʍıʅʅ qǝ sɐʌǝp "
"ɐs ǝxɐɯdʅǝ˙opʇ,˙  Noʇǝ ʇɥɐʇ „%s‮„ poǝs uoʇ ɹǝɟǝɹ ʇo ɐ dǝɹɔǝuʇɐƃǝ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:204
#, python-format
msgid ""
"In this message the variable is surrounded by double quotes. Make sure your "
"translation contains the variable %s and surround it similarly with quotes "
"in the way required by your language. If your language uses the same quotes "
"as English, type it exactly as shown for the English. If your language uses "
"different quoting characters you can just type them around the variable."
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʇɥǝ ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ ıs snɹɹonupǝp qʎ ponqʅǝ bnoʇǝs˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎonɹ "
"ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɔouʇɐıus ʇɥǝ ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ %s‮ ɐup snɹɹonup ıʇ sıɯıʅɐɹʅʎ ʍıʇɥ bnoʇǝs "
"ıu ʇɥǝ ʍɐʎ ɹǝbnıɹǝp qʎ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ˙ Iɟ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ nsǝs ʇɥǝ sɐɯǝ bnoʇǝs "
"ɐs Ǝuƃʅısɥ´ ʇʎdǝ ıʇ ǝxɐɔʇʅʎ ɐs sɥoʍu ɟoɹ ʇɥǝ Ǝuƃʅısɥ˙ Iɟ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ nsǝs "
"pıɟɟǝɹǝuʇ bnoʇıuƃ ɔɥɐɹɐɔʇǝɹs ʎon ɔɐu ɾnsʇ ʇʎdǝ ʇɥǝɯ ɐɹonup ʇɥǝ ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:213
msgid ""
"In this message, \"%(name)s\" is a placeholder (variable). Note that the 's' "
"is part of the variable, and the whole variable from '%' to the 's' should "
"appear unchanged somewhere in your translation. These type of variables give "
"you an idea of what they will contain. In this case, it will contain a name."
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ´ „%(name)s‮„ ıs ɐ dʅɐɔǝɥoʅpǝɹ (ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ)˙ Noʇǝ ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥǝ ,s, "
"ıs dɐɹʇ oɟ ʇɥǝ ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ´ ɐup ʇɥǝ ʍɥoʅǝ ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝ ɟɹoɯ ,%, ʇo ʇɥǝ ,s, sɥonʅp "
"ɐddǝɐɹ nuɔɥɐuƃǝp soɯǝʍɥǝɹǝ ıu ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou˙ ⊥ɥǝsǝ ʇʎdǝ oɟ ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝs ƃıʌǝ "
"ʎon ɐu ıpǝɐ oɟ ʍɥɐʇ ʇɥǝʎ ʍıʅʅ ɔouʇɐıu˙ Iu ʇɥıs ɔɐsǝ´ ıʇ ʍıʅʅ ɔouʇɐıu ɐ uɐɯǝ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:221
msgid ""
"In this message the user of the software is asked to do something. Make sure "
"you translate it by being as polite or respectful as is necessary for your "
"culture."
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʇɥǝ nsǝɹ oɟ ʇɥǝ soɟʇʍɐɹǝ ıs ɐsʞǝp ʇo po soɯǝʇɥıuƃ˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ "
"ʎon ʇɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ıʇ qʎ qǝıuƃ ɐs doʅıʇǝ oɹ ɹǝsdǝɔʇɟnʅ ɐs ıs uǝɔǝssɐɹʎ ɟoɹ ʎonɹ "
"ɔnʅʇnɹǝ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:227
msgid ""
"In this message there is reference to \"Linux\" (a product name). Many "
"languages will not translate it, but your language might use a "
"transliteration if you don't use the Latin script for your language."
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ʇɥǝɹǝ ıs ɹǝɟǝɹǝuɔǝ ʇo „⅂ıunx„ (ɐ dɹopnɔʇ uɐɯǝ)˙ Wɐuʎ "
"ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝs ʍıʅʅ uoʇ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ıʇ´ qnʇ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ ɯıƃɥʇ nsǝ ɐ "
"ʇɹɐusʅıʇǝɹɐʇıou ıɟ ʎon pou,ʇ nsǝ ʇɥǝ ⅂ɐʇıu sɔɹıdʇ ɟoɹ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:234
msgid ""
"This message contains the URL (web address) of the project website. It must "
"be transferred as a placeable or typed over exactly."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɔouʇɐıus ʇɥǝ ∩ᴚ⅂ (ʍǝq ɐppɹǝss) oɟ ʇɥǝ dɹoɾǝɔʇ ʍǝqsıʇǝ˙ Iʇ ɯnsʇ "
"qǝ ʇɹɐusɟǝɹɹǝp ɐs ɐ dʅɐɔǝɐqʅǝ oɹ ʇʎdǝp oʌǝɹ ǝxɐɔʇʅʎ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:239
msgid ""
"This message refers to a website with more information. Sometimes you might "
"be allowed or encouraged to change the URL (web address) to a website in "
"your language. In this case, replace the \"en\" at the start of the address "
"to your language code so that the address points to the corresponding "
"article in your language about XML."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɹǝɟǝɹs ʇo ɐ ʍǝqsıʇǝ ʍıʇɥ ɯoɹǝ ıuɟoɹɯɐʇıou˙ Soɯǝʇıɯǝs ʎon ɯıƃɥʇ "
"qǝ ɐʅʅoʍǝp oɹ ǝuɔonɹɐƃǝp ʇo ɔɥɐuƃǝ ʇɥǝ ∩ᴚ⅂ (ʍǝq ɐppɹǝss) ʇo ɐ ʍǝqsıʇǝ ıu "
"ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ˙ Iu ʇɥıs ɔɐsǝ´ ɹǝdʅɐɔǝ ʇɥǝ „ǝu„ ɐʇ ʇɥǝ sʇɐɹʇ oɟ ʇɥǝ ɐppɹǝss ʇo "
"ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ ɔopǝ so ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥǝ ɐppɹǝss doıuʇs ʇo ʇɥǝ ɔoɹɹǝsdoupıuƃ ɐɹʇıɔʅǝ "
"ıu ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ ɐqonʇ XW⅂˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:248
msgid ""
"This translation contains an ambiguous word - it has two possible meanings. "
"Make sure you can see the context information showing that this is a verb "
"(an action as in \"click here to view it\")."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɔouʇɐıus ɐu ɐɯqıƃnons ʍoɹp - ıʇ ɥɐs ʇʍo dossıqʅǝ ɯǝɐuıuƃs˙ "
"Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎon ɔɐu sǝǝ ʇɥǝ ɔouʇǝxʇ ıuɟoɹɯɐʇıou sɥoʍıuƃ ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥıs ıs ɐ ʌǝɹq "
"(ɐu ɐɔʇıou ɐs ıu „ɔʅıɔʞ ɥǝɹǝ ʇo ʌıǝʍ ıʇ„)˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:255
msgid ""
"This translation contains an ambiguous word - it has two possible meanings. "
"Make sure you can see the context information showing that this is a noun (a "
"thing as in \"click to change the view to full screen\"). If Virtaal gives "
"your previous translation as a suggestion, take care to only use it if it is "
"definitely appropriate in this case as well."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɔouʇɐıus ɐu ɐɯqıƃnons ʍoɹp - ıʇ ɥɐs ʇʍo dossıqʅǝ ɯǝɐuıuƃs˙ "
"Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎon ɔɐu sǝǝ ʇɥǝ ɔouʇǝxʇ ıuɟoɹɯɐʇıou sɥoʍıuƃ ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥıs ıs ɐ uonu (ɐ "
"ʇɥıuƃ ɐs ıu „ɔʅıɔʞ ʇo ɔɥɐuƃǝ ʇɥǝ ʌıǝʍ ʇo ɟnʅʅ sɔɹǝǝu„)˙ Iɟ Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ ƃıʌǝs "
"ʎonɹ dɹǝʌıons ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɐs ɐ snƃƃǝsʇıou´ ʇɐʞǝ ɔɐɹǝ ʇo ouʅʎ nsǝ ıʇ ıɟ ıʇ ıs "
"pǝɟıuıʇǝʅʎ ɐddɹodɹıɐʇǝ ıu ʇɥıs ɔɐsǝ ɐs ʍǝʅʅ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:264
msgid ""
"An accelerator key is a key on your keyboard that you can press to quickly "
"access a menu or function. It is also called a hot key, access key or "
"mnemonic. In program interfaces they are shown as an underlined letter in "
"the text label. In the translatable text they are marked using some "
"character like the underscore here, but other characters are used for this "
"as well. In this case the accelerator key is \"f\" since the underscore is "
"before this letter and it means that this accelerator could be triggered by "
"pressing Alt+F."
msgstr ""
"‮∀u ɐɔɔǝʅǝɹɐʇoɹ ʞǝʎ ıs ɐ ʞǝʎ ou ʎonɹ ʞǝʎqoɐɹp ʇɥɐʇ ʎon ɔɐu dɹǝss ʇo bnıɔʞʅʎ "
"ɐɔɔǝss ɐ ɯǝun oɹ ɟnuɔʇıou˙ Iʇ ıs ɐʅso ɔɐʅʅǝp ɐ ɥoʇ ʞǝʎ´ ɐɔɔǝss ʞǝʎ oɹ "
"ɯuǝɯouıɔ˙ Iu dɹoƃɹɐɯ ıuʇǝɹɟɐɔǝs ʇɥǝʎ ɐɹǝ sɥoʍu ɐs ɐu nupǝɹʅıuǝp ʅǝʇʇǝɹ ıu "
"ʇɥǝ ʇǝxʇ ʅɐqǝʅ˙ Iu ʇɥǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇɐqʅǝ ʇǝxʇ ʇɥǝʎ ɐɹǝ ɯɐɹʞǝp nsıuƃ soɯǝ "
"ɔɥɐɹɐɔʇǝɹ ʅıʞǝ ʇɥǝ nupǝɹsɔoɹǝ ɥǝɹǝ´ qnʇ oʇɥǝɹ ɔɥɐɹɐɔʇǝɹs ɐɹǝ nsǝp ɟoɹ ʇɥıs "
"ɐs ʍǝʅʅ˙ Iu ʇɥıs ɔɐsǝ ʇɥǝ ɐɔɔǝʅǝɹɐʇoɹ ʞǝʎ ıs „ɟ„ sıuɔǝ ʇɥǝ nupǝɹsɔoɹǝ ıs "
"qǝɟoɹǝ ʇɥıs ʅǝʇʇǝɹ ɐup ıʇ ɯǝɐus ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥıs ɐɔɔǝʅǝɹɐʇoɹ ɔonʅp qǝ ʇɹıƃƃǝɹǝp qʎ "
"dɹǝssıuƃ ∀ʅʇ+Ⅎ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:276
msgid "In this entry you can see other kind of accelerator."
msgstr "‮Iu ʇɥıs ǝuʇɹʎ ʎon ɔɐu sǝǝ oʇɥǝɹ ʞıup oɟ ɐɔɔǝʅǝɹɐʇoɹ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:280
msgid "And another kind of accelerator."
msgstr "‮∀up ɐuoʇɥǝɹ ʞıup oɟ ɐɔɔǝʅǝɹɐʇoɹ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:285
msgid ""
"Virtaal is able to provide suggestions from several terminology glossaries "
"and provides easy shortcuts to allow paste them in the translation field. "
"Right now Virtaal has only one empty terminology glossary, but you can start "
"filling it. In order to do that select the original text, press Ctrl+T, "
"provide a translation for your language."
msgstr ""
"‮Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ ıs ɐqʅǝ ʇo dɹoʌıpǝ snƃƃǝsʇıous ɟɹoɯ sǝʌǝɹɐʅ ʇǝɹɯıuoʅoƃʎ ƃʅossɐɹıǝs "
"ɐup dɹoʌıpǝs ǝɐsʎ sɥoɹʇɔnʇs ʇo ɐʅʅoʍ dɐsʇǝ ʇɥǝɯ ıu ʇɥǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɟıǝʅp˙ "
"ᴚıƃɥʇ uoʍ Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ ɥɐs ouʅʎ ouǝ ǝɯdʇʎ ʇǝɹɯıuoʅoƃʎ ƃʅossɐɹʎ´ qnʇ ʎon ɔɐu sʇɐɹʇ "
"ɟıʅʅıuƃ ıʇ˙ Iu oɹpǝɹ ʇo po ʇɥɐʇ sǝʅǝɔʇ ʇɥǝ oɹıƃıuɐʅ ʇǝxʇ´ dɹǝss Ↄʇɹʅ+⊥´ "
"dɹoʌıpǝ ɐ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɟoɹ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:295
msgid ""
"In the previous entry you have created one terminology entry for the "
"\"filter\" verb. Now do the same for \"filter\" noun."
msgstr ""
"‮Iu ʇɥǝ dɹǝʌıons ǝuʇɹʎ ʎon ɥɐʌǝ ɔɹǝɐʇǝp ouǝ ʇǝɹɯıuoʅoƃʎ ǝuʇɹʎ ɟoɹ ʇɥǝ „ɟıʅʇǝɹ"
"„ ʌǝɹq˙ Noʍ po ʇɥǝ sɐɯǝ ɟoɹ „ɟıʅʇǝɹ„ uonu˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:300
msgid ""
"If you have created any terminology in the previous entries you may now see "
"some of the words with a green background (or other color depending on your "
"theme). This means that Virtaal has terminology suggestions for that word. "
"Use Alt+Right to select the highlighted word, and then press Alt+Down. If "
"only one suggestion is provided then Alt+Down just copies the suggestion to "
"the translation field. But if several suggestions are available Alt+Down "
"shows a suggestion list which you can navigate using Down and Up keys. Once "
"you have selected the desired suggestion press Enter to copy it to the "
"translation field."
msgstr ""
"‮Iɟ ʎon ɥɐʌǝ ɔɹǝɐʇǝp ɐuʎ ʇǝɹɯıuoʅoƃʎ ıu ʇɥǝ dɹǝʌıons ǝuʇɹıǝs ʎon ɯɐʎ uoʍ sǝǝ "
"soɯǝ oɟ ʇɥǝ ʍoɹps ʍıʇɥ ɐ ƃɹǝǝu qɐɔʞƃɹonup (oɹ oʇɥǝɹ ɔoʅoɹ pǝdǝupıuƃ ou ʎonɹ "
"ʇɥǝɯǝ)˙ ⊥ɥıs ɯǝɐus ʇɥɐʇ Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ ɥɐs ʇǝɹɯıuoʅoƃʎ snƃƃǝsʇıous ɟoɹ ʇɥɐʇ ʍoɹp˙ ∩"
"sǝ ∀ʅʇ+ᴚıƃɥʇ ʇo sǝʅǝɔʇ ʇɥǝ ɥıƃɥʅıƃɥʇǝp ʍoɹp´ ɐup ʇɥǝu dɹǝss ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu˙ Iɟ "
"ouʅʎ ouǝ snƃƃǝsʇıou ıs dɹoʌıpǝp ʇɥǝu ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu ɾnsʇ ɔodıǝs ʇɥǝ snƃƃǝsʇıou ʇo "
"ʇɥǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɟıǝʅp˙ Ԑnʇ ıɟ sǝʌǝɹɐʅ snƃƃǝsʇıous ɐɹǝ ɐʌɐıʅɐqʅǝ ∀ʅʇ+ᗡoʍu "
"sɥoʍs ɐ snƃƃǝsʇıou ʅısʇ ʍɥıɔɥ ʎon ɔɐu uɐʌıƃɐʇǝ nsıuƃ ᗡoʍu ɐup ∩d ʞǝʎs˙ Ouɔǝ "
"ʎon ɥɐʌǝ sǝʅǝɔʇǝp ʇɥǝ pǝsıɹǝp snƃƃǝsʇıou dɹǝss Ǝuʇǝɹ ʇo ɔodʎ ıʇ ʇo ʇɥǝ "
"ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɟıǝʅp˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:313
msgid ""
"This message has two lines. Make sure that your translation also contains "
"two lines. You can separate lines with Shift+Enter or copy newline "
"placeables (displayed as ¶)."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɥɐs ʇʍo ʅıuǝs˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʇɥɐʇ ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɐʅso ɔouʇɐıus "
"ʇʍo ʅıuǝs˙ ⅄on ɔɐu sǝdɐɹɐʇǝ ʅıuǝs ʍıʇɥ Sɥıɟʇ+Ǝuʇǝɹ oɹ ɔodʎ uǝʍʅıuǝ "
"dʅɐɔǝɐqʅǝs (pısdʅɐʎǝp ɐs ¶)˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:320
msgid ""
"This message contains tab characters to separate some headings. Make sure "
"you separate your translations in the same way."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɔouʇɐıus ʇɐq ɔɥɐɹɐɔʇǝɹs ʇo sǝdɐɹɐʇǝ soɯǝ ɥǝɐpıuƃs˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ "
"ʎon sǝdɐɹɐʇǝ ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıous ıu ʇɥǝ sɐɯǝ ʍɐʎ˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:325
msgid ""
"This message contains a large number that is formatted according to the "
"American convention. Translate this but make sure to format the number "
"according to your language's convention. You might need to change the comma "
"(,) and full stop (.) to other characters, and you also might need to use a "
"different number system. Make sure that you understand the American "
"formatting: this number is bigger than one thousand."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɔouʇɐıus ɐ ʅɐɹƃǝ unɯqǝɹ ʇɥɐʇ ıs ɟoɹɯɐʇʇǝp ɐɔɔoɹpıuƃ ʇo ʇɥǝ ∀"
"ɯǝɹıɔɐu ɔouʌǝuʇıou˙ ⊥ɹɐusʅɐʇǝ ʇɥıs qnʇ ɯɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʇo ɟoɹɯɐʇ ʇɥǝ unɯqǝɹ "
"ɐɔɔoɹpıuƃ ʇo ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ,s ɔouʌǝuʇıou˙ ⅄on ɯıƃɥʇ uǝǝp ʇo ɔɥɐuƃǝ ʇɥǝ ɔoɯɯɐ "
"(´) ɐup ɟnʅʅ sʇod (˙) ʇo oʇɥǝɹ ɔɥɐɹɐɔʇǝɹs´ ɐup ʎon ɐʅso ɯıƃɥʇ uǝǝp ʇo nsǝ ɐ "
"pıɟɟǝɹǝuʇ unɯqǝɹ sʎsʇǝɯ˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʇɥɐʇ ʎon nupǝɹsʇɐup ʇɥǝ ∀ɯǝɹıɔɐu "
"ɟoɹɯɐʇʇıuƃ: ʇɥıs unɯqǝɹ ıs qıƃƃǝɹ ʇɥɐu ouǝ ʇɥonsɐup˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:335
msgid ""
"This message refers to miles. If the programmers encourage it, you might "
"want to change this to kilometres in your translation, if kilometers are "
"more commonly used in your language. Note that 1 mile is about 1.6 "
"kilometres. Note that automated tests for \"numbers\" will complain if the "
"number is changed, but in this case it is safe to do so."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɹǝɟǝɹs ʇo ɯıʅǝs˙ Iɟ ʇɥǝ dɹoƃɹɐɯɯǝɹs ǝuɔonɹɐƃǝ ıʇ´ ʎon ɯıƃɥʇ "
"ʍɐuʇ ʇo ɔɥɐuƃǝ ʇɥıs ʇo ʞıʅoɯǝʇɹǝs ıu ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou´ ıɟ ʞıʅoɯǝʇǝɹs ɐɹǝ "
"ɯoɹǝ ɔoɯɯouʅʎ nsǝp ıu ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ˙ Noʇǝ ʇɥɐʇ 1‮ ɯıʅǝ ıs ɐqonʇ 1.6‮ ʞıʅoɯǝʇɹǝs"
"˙ Noʇǝ ʇɥɐʇ ɐnʇoɯɐʇǝp ʇǝsʇs ɟoɹ „unɯqǝɹs„ ʍıʅʅ ɔoɯdʅɐıu ıɟ ʇɥǝ unɯqǝɹ ıs "
"ɔɥɐuƃǝp´ qnʇ ıu ʇɥıs ɔɐsǝ ıʇ ıs sɐɟǝ ʇo po so˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:344
msgid ""
"This message contains a link that the user will be able to click on to visit "
"the help page. Make sure you correctly keep the information between the "
"angle brackets (<...>). The double quotes (\") should never be changed in "
"tags, even if your language uses a different type of quotation marks."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɔouʇɐıus ɐ ʅıuʞ ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥǝ nsǝɹ ʍıʅʅ qǝ ɐqʅǝ ʇo ɔʅıɔʞ ou ʇo ʌısıʇ "
"ʇɥǝ ɥǝʅd dɐƃǝ˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎon ɔoɹɹǝɔʇʅʎ ʞǝǝd ʇɥǝ ıuɟoɹɯɐʇıou qǝʇʍǝǝu ʇɥǝ "
"ɐuƃʅǝ qɹɐɔʞǝʇs (<...>‮)˙ ⊥ɥǝ ponqʅǝ bnoʇǝs („) sɥonʅp uǝʌǝɹ qǝ ɔɥɐuƃǝp ıu ʇɐƃs"
"´ ǝʌǝu ıɟ ʎonɹ ʅɐuƃnɐƃǝ nsǝs ɐ pıɟɟǝɹǝuʇ ʇʎdǝ oɟ bnoʇɐʇıou ɯɐɹʞs˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:354
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This message contains a similar link, but the programmers decided to rather "
"insert the tags by using variables so that translators can't change them. "
"Make sure you position the two variables (%s) so that they correspond to the "
"opening and closing tags of the previous translation."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɔouʇɐıus ɐ sıɯıʅɐɹ ʅıuʞ´ qnʇ ʇɥǝ dɹoƃɹɐɯɯǝɹs pǝɔıpǝp ʇo ɹɐʇɥǝɹ "
"ıusǝɹʇ ʇɥǝ ʇɐƃs qʎ nsıuƃ ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝs so ʇɥɐʇ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇoɹs ɔɐu,ʇ ɔɥɐuƃǝ ʇɥǝɯ˙ "
"Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎon dosıʇıou ʇɥǝ ʇʍo ʌɐɹıɐqʅǝs (%s‮) so ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥǝʎ ɔoɹɹǝsdoup ʇo ʇɥǝ "
"odǝuıuƃ ɐup ɔʅosıuƃ ʇɐƃs oɟ ʇɥǝ dɹǝʌıons ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:362
msgid ""
"This message contains the <b> and </b> tags to emphasize a word, while "
"everything is within the <p> and </p> tags. Make sure your whole translation "
"is within the <p> and </p> tags."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɔouʇɐıus ʇɥǝ <b>‮ ɐup </b>‮ ʇɐƃs ʇo ǝɯdɥɐsızǝ ɐ ʍoɹp´ ʍɥıʅǝ "
"ǝʌǝɹʎʇɥıuƃ ıs ʍıʇɥıu ʇɥǝ <p>‮ ɐup </p>‮ ʇɐƃs˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎonɹ ʍɥoʅǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou "
"ıs ʍıʇɥıu ʇɥǝ <p>‮ ɐup </p>‮ ʇɐƃs˙"

#: ../virtaal/support/tutorial.py:368
msgid ""
"This message contains a similar link that is contained within <span> and </"
"span>. Make sure you correctly keep all the tags (<...>), and that the link "
"is completely contained within the <span> and </span> tags in your "
"translation. Make sure that the text inside the \"a\" tags correspond to "
"\"help page\" and that your translation corresponding to the second sentence "
"is contained in the <span> tags. Note how the full stop is still inside the "
"</span> tag."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥıs ɯǝssɐƃǝ ɔouʇɐıus ɐ sıɯıʅɐɹ ʅıuʞ ʇɥɐʇ ıs ɔouʇɐıuǝp ʍıʇɥıu <span>‮ ɐup </"
"span>‮˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʎon ɔoɹɹǝɔʇʅʎ ʞǝǝd ɐʅʅ ʇɥǝ ʇɐƃs (<...>‮)´ ɐup ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥǝ ʅıuʞ "
"ıs ɔoɯdʅǝʇǝʅʎ ɔouʇɐıuǝp ʍıʇɥıu ʇɥǝ <span>‮ ɐup </span>‮ ʇɐƃs ıu ʎonɹ "
"ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou˙ Wɐʞǝ snɹǝ ʇɥɐʇ ʇɥǝ ʇǝxʇ ıusıpǝ ʇɥǝ „ɐ„ ʇɐƃs ɔoɹɹǝsdoup ʇo „ɥǝʅd "
"dɐƃǝ„ ɐup ʇɥɐʇ ʎonɹ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou ɔoɹɹǝsdoupıuƃ ʇo ʇɥǝ sǝɔoup sǝuʇǝuɔǝ ıs "
"ɔouʇɐıuǝp ıu ʇɥǝ <span>‮ ʇɐƃs˙ Noʇǝ ɥoʍ ʇɥǝ ɟnʅʅ sʇod ıs sʇıʅʅ ıusıpǝ ʇɥǝ </"
"span>‮ ʇɐƃ˙"

#: ../virtaal/views/checksunitview.py:72
msgid "No issues"
msgstr "‮No ıssnǝs"

#: ../virtaal/views/checksunitview.py:79
msgid "Quality Check"
msgstr "‮Ònɐʅıʇʎ Ↄɥǝɔʞ"

#: ../virtaal/views/checksunitview.py:85
msgid "Description"
msgstr "‮ᗡǝsɔɹıdʇıou"

#: ../virtaal/views/checksprojview.py:39
msgid "Project Type"
msgstr "‮Ԁɹoɾǝɔʇ ⊥ʎdǝ"

#. l10n: The label indicating the checker style (GNOME/KDE/whatever)
#: ../virtaal/views/checksprojview.py:65
#, python-format
msgid "Checks: %(checker_name)s"
msgstr "‮Ↄɥǝɔʞs: %(checker_name)s"

#: ../virtaal/views/langview.py:73
msgid "_New Language Pair..."
msgstr "‮_Nǝʍ ⅂ɐuƃnɐƃǝ Ԁɐıɹ˙˙˙"

#: ../virtaal/views/mainview.py:244
msgid "Error"
msgstr "‮Ǝɹɹoɹ"

#: ../virtaal/views/mainview.py:356
msgid ""
"The current file has been modified.\n"
"Do you want to save your changes?"
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥǝ ɔnɹɹǝuʇ ɟıʅǝ ɥɐs qǝǝu ɯopıɟıǝp˙\n"
"‮ᗡo ʎon ʍɐuʇ ʇo sɐʌǝ ʎonɹ ɔɥɐuƃǝs¿"

#: ../virtaal/views/mainview.py:359
msgid "_Discard"
msgstr "‮_ᗡısɔɐɹp"

#. l10n: This is the title of the main window of Virtaal
#. %(modified_marker)s is a star that is displayed if the file is modified, and should be at the start of the window title
#. %(current_file)s is the file name of the current file
#. most languages will not need to change this
#: ../virtaal/views/mainview.py:444
#, python-format
msgid "%(modified_marker)s%(current_file)s - Virtaal"
msgstr "%(modified_marker)s%(current_file)s‮ - Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ"

#: ../virtaal/views/mainview.py:469
msgid "Please enter the number of noun forms (plurals) to use"
msgstr "‮Ԁʅǝɐsǝ ǝuʇǝɹ ʇɥǝ unɯqǝɹ oɟ uonu ɟoɹɯs (dʅnɹɐʅs) ʇo nsǝ"

#: ../virtaal/views/mainview.py:475
msgid "Please enter the plural equation to use"
msgstr "‮Ԁʅǝɐsǝ ǝuʇǝɹ ʇɥǝ dʅnɹɐʅ ǝbnɐʇıou ʇo nsǝ"

#. l10n: This refers to the 'mode' that determines how Virtaal moves
#. between units.
#: ../virtaal/views/modeview.py:61
msgid "N_avigation:"
msgstr "‮N_ɐʌıƃɐʇıou:"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:32
msgid "Untranslated:"
msgstr "‮∩uʇɹɐusʅɐʇǝp:"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:33
msgid "Needs work:"
msgstr "‮Nǝǝps ʍoɹʞ:"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:34
msgid "Rejected:"
msgstr "‮ᴚǝɾǝɔʇǝp:"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:35
msgid "Needs review:"
msgstr "‮Nǝǝps ɹǝʌıǝʍ:"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:36
msgid "Translated:"
msgstr "‮⊥ɹɐusʅɐʇǝp:"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:37
msgid "Reviewed:"
msgstr "‮ᴚǝʌıǝʍǝp:"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:59
msgid "(0%)"
msgstr "‮(0‮%)"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:61
msgid "(100%)"
msgstr "‮(100‮%)"

#. l10n: This is the formatting for percentages in the file properties. If unsure, just copy the original.
#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:64
#, python-format
msgid "(%04.1f%%)"
msgstr "‮(%04.1f%%‮)"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:134
msgid "Save the file for up-to-date information"
msgstr "‮Sɐʌǝ ʇɥǝ ɟıʅǝ ɟoɹ nd-ʇo-pɐʇǝ ıuɟoɹɯɐʇıou"

#. l10n: The total number of words. You can not use %Id at this stage. If unsure, just copy the original.
#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:191
#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:192
#, python-format
msgid "<b>%d</b>"
msgstr "<b>%d</b>"

#: ../virtaal/views/propertiesview.py:203
#, python-format
msgid "%.1f KB"
msgstr "%.1f‮ ӼԐ"

#: ../virtaal/views/storeview.py:142 ../virtaal/views/storeview.py:151
msgid "Export failed"
msgstr "‮Ǝxdoɹʇ ɟɐıʅǝp"

#: ../virtaal/views/storeview.py:160
msgid "Preview failed"
msgstr "‮Ԁɹǝʌıǝʍ ɟɐıʅǝp"

#: ../virtaal/views/unitview.py:612
msgid "Move one step back in the workflow (Ctrl+Shift+Enter)"
msgstr "‮Woʌǝ ouǝ sʇǝd qɐɔʞ ıu ʇɥǝ ʍoɹʞɟʅoʍ (Ↄʇɹʅ+Sɥıɟʇ+Ǝuʇǝɹ)"

#: ../virtaal/views/unitview.py:613
msgid "Click to move to a specific state in the workflow"
msgstr "‮Ↄʅıɔʞ ʇo ɯoʌǝ ʇo ɐ sdǝɔıɟıɔ sʇɐʇǝ ıu ʇɥǝ ʍoɹʞɟʅoʍ"

#: ../virtaal/views/unitview.py:614
msgid "Move one step forward in the workflow (Ctrl+Enter)"
msgstr "‮Woʌǝ ouǝ sʇǝd ɟoɹʍɐɹp ıu ʇɥǝ ʍoɹʞɟʅoʍ (Ↄʇɹʅ+Ǝuʇǝɹ)"

#: ../virtaal/views/widgets/aboutdialog.py:34
msgid "Copyright © 2007-2010 Zuza Software Foundation"
msgstr "‮Ↄodʎɹıƃɥʇ ©‮ 2007-2010‮ Znzɐ Soɟʇʍɐɹǝ Ⅎonupɐʇıou"

#. l10n: Please retain the literal name "Virtaal", but feel free to
#. additionally transliterate the name and to add a translation of "For Language", which is what the name means.
#: ../virtaal/views/widgets/aboutdialog.py:37
msgid "Virtaal is a program for doing translation."
msgstr "‮Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ ıs ɐ dɹoƃɹɐɯ ɟoɹ poıuƃ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou˙"

#: ../virtaal/views/widgets/aboutdialog.py:38
msgid ""
"The initial focus is on software translation (localization or l10n), but we "
"definitely intend it to be useful as a general purpose tool for Computer "
"Aided Translation (CAT)."
msgstr ""
"‮⊥ɥǝ ıuıʇıɐʅ ɟoɔns ıs ou soɟʇʍɐɹǝ ʇɹɐusʅɐʇıou (ʅoɔɐʅızɐʇıou oɹ ʅ10‮u)´ qnʇ ʍǝ "
"pǝɟıuıʇǝʅʎ ıuʇǝup ıʇ ʇo qǝ nsǝɟnʅ ɐs ɐ ƃǝuǝɹɐʅ dnɹdosǝ ʇooʅ ɟoɹ Ↄoɯdnʇǝɹ ∀"
"ıpǝp ⊥ɹɐusʅɐʇıou (Ↄ∀⊥)˙"

#: ../virtaal/views/widgets/aboutdialog.py:52
msgid "Virtaal website"
msgstr "‮Ʌıɹʇɐɐʅ ʍǝqsıʇǝ"

#: ../virtaal/views/widgets/aboutdialog.py:65
msgid "We thank our donors:"
msgstr "‮Ｍǝ ʇɥɐuʞ onɹ pouoɹs:"

#: ../virtaal/views/widgets/aboutdialog.py:66
